{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJp1qvgYS3nmRDu2wH7y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ccode(sinc(x))` now produces valid C:\n\n```c\n((x != 0) ? (\n   sin(x)/x\n)\n: (\n   1\n))\n```\n\nThe Piecewise example from the issue now prints `x != 0` instead of `Ne(x, 0)`.\n\nThere were two problems. The C printer had no rule for `sinc`, so it fell through to \"Not supported\". And conditions like `Ne(x, 0)` were printed in SymPy's own text form, which isn't valid C.\n\nI changed only `sympy/printing/ccode.py` and added two methods:\n- **`_print_sinc`** rewrites `sinc(x)` as `Piecewise((sin(x)/x, Ne(x, 0)), (1, True))` and prints that.\n- **`_print_Relational`** prints comparisons as `lhs op rhs`, so you get `x != 0`, `x < y` and so on. This changes how every comparison appears in C output, not just inside `sinc`.\n\nThe repro script now gives the output above. The existing tests in `sympy/printing/tests/test_ccode.py` and `sympy/utilities/tests/test_codegen.py` pass (81 passed). I didn't add new tests, since the rules don't allow editing test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2181,"cache_read_input_tokens":21141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2181},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ba0b466-b164-4b37-b851-e14b9298a659","uuid":"8ba5373e-134f-45b2-812f-b6d53de3993c","timestamp":"2026-11-22T23:11:03.406Z","request_id":"req_011ChJp1qkG3W9cX6JazaBRc"}
